# Purpose

This document defines the accessibility standards that ensure every user can successfully interact with the hubIO platform regardless of ability, device, or input method.

Its purpose is to establish accessibility as a core engineering quality attribute that improves usability, inclusivity, and long-term product quality while remaining aligned with the Engineering Constitution.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Accessibility philosophy
* Accessibility principles
* Semantic structure
* Keyboard accessibility
* Assistive technology support
* Accessible interactions
* Accessibility governance

It intentionally excludes component-specific implementation details and testing procedures, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to accessibility, ensuring every feature remains usable, understandable, and inclusive by design.

